Here's a well-structured prompt you can use:
Prompt
You are an expert Java developer with deep knowledge of Micro Focus ALM Octane REST APIs and TestNG frameworks.
Context:
I have a Selenium Java TestNG framework that generates a testng-results.xml file after test execution. I need to programmatically integrate this with ALM Octane using Java and Octane's REST APIs.
Assumptions:
Octane is already set up with a valid server URL, shared space ID, and workspace ID
A Product Area already exists in Octane
A Test Suite already exists in Octane
Authentication credentials (client ID + client secret) are available
Task — implement the following flow in Java, in order:
1. Authentication
Authenticate with Octane using client ID and client secret via the /authentication/sign_in endpoint
Store and reuse the LWSSO_COOKIE_KEY session cookie for all subsequent API calls
2. Parse testng-results.xml
Parse the TestNG results XML file using a Java XML parser (e.g. JAXB or DOM)
Extract: test name, class name, method name, status (PASS/FAIL/SKIP), duration, and any failure messages
3. Create Automated Tests (AT) inside the existing Test Suite
For each unique test method found in the XML, create an Automated Test (AT) entity in Octane under the existing Test Suite
Map the test class and method name appropriately
Set the test type to Automated and link to the existing Product Area
Use POST /api/shared_spaces/{shared_space_id}/workspaces/{workspace_id}/tests
4. Create a Suite Run
Create a Suite Run entity in Octane linked to the existing Test Suite
Set the run name, start time, and status based on the overall XML results
Use POST /api/shared_spaces/{shared_space_id}/workspaces/{workspace_id}/suite_runs
5. Create Automated Runs (AR) inside the Suite Run
For each test result in the XML, create an Automated Run (AR) entity inside the Suite Run created in step 4
Map status: passed, failed, skipped
Link each AR to the corresponding AT created in step 3
Include duration and failure message where applicable
Use POST /api/shared_spaces/{shared_space_id}/workspaces/{workspace_id}/runs
6. Upload Attachments to the Suite Run
Upload the testng-results.xml (and optionally any screenshots or logs) as attachments to the Suite Run created above
Use POST /api/shared_spaces/{shared_space_id}/workspaces/{workspace_id}/attachments
Send as multipart/form-data with the entity type and ID referencing the Suite Run
Technical Requirements:
Language: Java 11+
HTTP Client: HttpClient (native Java 11) or Apache HttpClient
JSON library: org.json or Jackson
XML parsing: DOM or JAXB
Structure the code into clean, separate classes:
OctaneAuthenticator.java — handles login and cookie management
TestNGResultsParser.java — parses the XML and returns a list of test result POJOs
OctaneTestCreator.java — creates ATs in Octane
OctaneSuiteRunCreator.java — creates Suite Run and ARs
OctaneAttachmentUploader.java — handles file attachment upload
OctaneIntegrationRunner.java — main orchestrator class
Include all JSON request payload examples for each API call
Include error handling (HTTP status checks, meaningful exceptions)
Add inline comments explaining each API interaction
Output expected:
Complete, runnable Java source code for all classes above
Sample JSON payloads for each Octane REST API request
Maven pom.xml with required dependencies
A brief explanation of the entity relationships: Test Suite → AT → Suite Run → AR → Attachments
